==Special attack==
[[File:Disrupt.gif|thumb|250px|A player performing the Voidwaker's special attack, ''Disrupt''.]]
The Voidwaker has a [[special attack]], ''Disrupt'', which consumes 50% of the player's special attack energy. The special attack deals [[successful hit|guaranteed]] Magic damage between 50-150% of the wielder's maximum melee hit. The special attack will provide 2 Magic experience per damage dealt.

The special attack is particularly useful due to its guaranteed medium to high damage. In [[Player killing|PvP]], it can be used for a consistent finishing blow and it pairs well with other high-damage special attack weapons such as the [[Armadyl godsword|Armadyl]] or [[ancient godsword]], [[dragon claws]], or [[granite maul]] due to its special attack cost. 

In PvM situations, the voidwaker is strongest when facing an enemy with high melee defence (such as high slash when using claws) and is not immune or resistant to magic damage. Compared to the [[crimson kisten]], the voidwaker's guaranteed accuracy and higher strength bonus makes it superior against enemies resistant to crush, but it will generally perform slightly worse on average than it when facing crush-susceptible enemies, as the voidwaker has a minimum of 50% and maximum of 150%, whereas the kisten has a minimum of 70-110% on one roll or 130-170% on four rolls.

